dmap is intact.'\\n    Quote: NVIDIA publicly disputed the report on Monday, with a spokesperson telling Bloomberg its “roadmap is intact.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e92 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected the SemiAnalysis report that its Kyber/Rubin Ultra roadmap had slipped, stating 'Our roadmap is intact.'\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e108, e124, e168, e180, e195, e211, e252; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e251 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis (X post), reported by Futuriom; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] Research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks; the article says this could push NVIDIA to use its new credit/revenue-sharing model to sustain demand.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s stock also suffered this week because research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks—a situation that could be further impetus for NVIDIA to deploy its new credit and revenue-sharing model, creating a continuing flow of demand for its products.\",\n   \"- e252 [party_statement; NVIDIA spokesperson; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] An NVIDIA spokesperson said 'Our road map is intact' and that 'Vera Rubin Ultra will scale up to a larger NVL576 domain in its planned 2027 timeline,' responding to reported Kyber NVL144 setbacks.\\n    Quote: An NVIDIA spokesperson said, “Our road map is intact.” Further, \\\"Vera Rubin Ultra will scale up to a larger NVL576 domain in its planned 2027 timeline.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e90 [third_party_view; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Research firm SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale architecture — the server cabinet designed to pack 144 GPUs and slated to debut with NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin Ultra system in 2027 — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, because the multi-layer PCB midplane at the heart of the system 'remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint.' SemiAnalysis also said the larger NVL576 system, which links eight racks via optical connections, is likely delayed or limited to small volumes.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap. … The setback stems from difficulties manufacturing a key circuit board at the heart of the syst\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e106, e122, e164, e167, e171, e175, e177, e194, e210, e305; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e305 [rumour; barchart.com; original source  ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Unnamed reports suggested that Nvidia's next-generation Kyber rack-scale AI infrastructure could be delayed until 2028, against a prior expectation that it would launch in 2027.\\n    Quote: Recently, Nvidia faced reports that suggested its next-generation Kyber rack-scale AI infrastructure could be delayed until 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e90; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e306 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia denied speculation that its Kyber rack-scale AI infrastructure is delayed, maintaining that its roadmap remains on track; the article states Kyber, designed for the Rubin Ultra platform, is expected to launch in 2027 as an integrated AI infrastructure system.\\n    Quote: However, the company denied the speculation, maintaining that its roadmap remains on track. Designed for the Rubin Ultra platform, Kyber is expected to launch in 2027 as an integrated AI infrastructure system and a key component of Nvidia's long-term AI infrastructure strategy.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e339; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e134 (); both are in force: NVIDIA shares were reported to be under pressure on reports of delays across its upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems; the reports are unattributed in the article.\",\n   \"- e319 [party_statement; IEEE Spectrum (Knvul Sheikh); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a4eb2bdfabca94f5887881c6 2026-07-09] Nvidia plans to add even more processors to single interconnected systems, going from 72 GPUs today to as many as 576 by 2027, as it scales its rack-scale systems, according to IEEE Spectrum.\\n    Quote: At the same time, Nvidia is planning to add even more processors to single interconnected systems, going from 72 GPUs today to as many as 576 by 2027.\",\n   \"- e339 [party_statement; Bloomberg (via moomoo); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Nvidia issued a statement to Bloomberg denying claims of a technical delay and confirming that its product roadmap remains intact, a clarification the article says counters concerns that infrastructure bottlenecks could disrupt its AI competitive lead.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA recently issued a statement to Bloomberg denying claims of a technical delay, confirming that its product roadmap remains intact. Thi