enial against reports of a delay to its next generation AI chips.\\n    Quote: AI giant NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) is currently in the news these days due to reports of a delay to its next generation AI chips. … NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) has denied reports that the Kyber platform is being delayed.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e306; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e90 [third_party_view; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Research firm SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale architecture — the server cabinet designed to pack 144 GPUs and slated to debut with NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin Ultra system in 2027 — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, because the multi-layer PCB midplane at the heart of the system 'remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint.' SemiAnalysis also said the larger NVL576 system, which links eight racks via optical connections, is likely delayed or limited to small volumes.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap. … The setback stems from difficulties manufacturing a key circuit board at the heart of the syst\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e106, e122, e164, e167, e171, e175, e177, e194, e210, e305, e423; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e92 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected the SemiAnalysis report that its Kyber/Rubin Ultra roadmap had slipped, stating 'Our roadmap is intact.'\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e108, e124, e168, e180, e195, e211, e252, e424; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e423 [third_party_view; Geoffrey Seiler, fool.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 next-generation AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 because of problems manufacturing a crucial circuit board.\\n    Quote: This has been a key part of CEO Jensen Huang's strategy; however, it could have hit a snag when technology research outfit SemiAnalysis reported that its Kyber NVL144 next-gen AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 due to troubles with manufacturing a crucial circuit board.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e90; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e424 [party_statement; Geoffrey Seiler, fool.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] Nvidia said its roadmap remains intact, responding to the SemiAnalysis report that the Kyber NVL144 next-generation AI rack system could be delayed until 2028, though the article says questions linger.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has come out and said its roadmap remains intact, although questions linger.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e251 (); both are in force: Research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks; the article says this could push NVIDIA to use its new credit/revenue-sharing model to sustain demand.\",\n   \"- e434 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] In investor-relations discussions, NVIDIA said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule and confirmed there have been no changes to its NVLink architecture.\\n    Quote: The company said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule and confirmed there have been no changes to its NVLink architecture.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e134 (); both are in force: NVIDIA shares were reported to be under pressure on reports of delays across its upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems; the reports are unattributed in the article.\",\n   \"- e90 [third_party_view; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Research firm SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale architecture — the server cabinet designed to pack 144 GPUs and slated to debut with NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin Ultra system in 2027 — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, because the multi-layer PCB midplane at the heart of the system 'remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint.' SemiAnalysis also said the larger NVL576 system, which links eight racks via optical connections, is likely delayed or limited to small volumes.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap. … The setback stems from difficulties manufacturing a key circuit board at the heart of the syst\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e106, e122, e164, e167, e171, e175, e177, e194, e210, e305, e423, e532; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e92 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected the SemiAnalysis report that its Kyber/Rubin Ultra roadmap had slipped, stating 'Our roadmap is intact.'\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e108, e124, e168, e180, e195, e211, e252, e424, e533; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e532 [third_party_view; EBC (ebc.com); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Industry research firm SemiAnalysis reported over the weekend before the 2026-07-14 article that Nvidia's upcoming Kyber NVL144 architecture could face delays extending into 2028.\\n    Quote: Over the weekend, reports circulated from industry research firm SemiAnalysis suggesting that Nvidia’s upcoming Kyber NVL144 architecture could face delays extending into 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e90; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e533 [party_statement; EBC (ebc.com); original source NVIDIA Corp. (spokesperson) ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] An Nvidia spokesperson countered SemiAnalysis's report on a Kyber NVL144 delay, saying the company's \\\"roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Quote: Although an Nvidia spokesperson quickly countered the reports, telling that the company's \\\"roadmap is intact,\\\" the seeds of doubt were already sown.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
