{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/controls/control-packet-6.json\\\"));\nfor x in p[1:3]:\n print(\\\"CONTROL\\\",x[\\\"control\\\"])\n for e in x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"]:\n  if any(s in e.lower() for s in [\\\"sold out\\\",\\\"less powerful\\\",\\\"accelerating growth\\\",\\\"100 billion\\\", \\\"\"'$100 bn\", \"100 bn\"]): print(e)'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"CONTROL 22\nCONTROL 23\n- e514 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Broadcom (Hock Tan, CEO) ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] Broadcom CEO Hock Tan said momentum continues, with fiscal Q3 AI semiconductor revenue set to grow more than 200% year over year to $16 billion; Broadcom guided total Q3 revenue to $29.4 billion (+84% YoY), set a stated goal of exceeding $100 billion in AI sales by 2027, and reported AI semiconductor revenue of $10.8 billion last quarter, up 143% YoY — custom AI silicon revenue that competes for the same AI data-center spending as NVIDIA, per 247wallst.com's 2026-07-14 article.\n    Quote: Broadcom’s Hock Tan says “the momentum continues” with Q3 AI semi revenue set to grow over 200% year-over-year to $16 billion. … Broadcom guided Q3 revenue to $29.4B (+84% YoY), and management’s stated goal is to exceed $100B in AI sales by 2027. AI semi revenue grew 143% YoY to $10.8B last quarter.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e136; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"control\":21,\"same_question\":\"no\",\"same_due\":\"yes\",\"items\":{\"i105\":\"shown\",\"i219\":\"shown\",\"i202\":\"shown\",\"i207\":\"shown\"},\"why\":\"The judged question requires NVIDIA to confirm customer shipments through specified channels, while the ruler asks whether shipping began.\"}\n{\"control\":22,\"same_question\":\"no\",\"same_due\":\"yes\",\"items\":{\"i270\":\"shown\",\"i304\":\"shown\",\"i305\":\"not_shown\",\"i309\":\"shown\"},\"why\":\"The judged question permits NVIDIA-confirmed shipments or revenue to count without a public Chinese authorization, and i305's sold-out domestic suppliers and buyers considering less powerful chips are absent.\"}\n{\"control\":23,\"same_question\":\"yes\",\"same_due\":\"yes\",\"items\":{\"i256\":\"shown\",\"i232\":\"shown\",\"i233\":\"shown\",\"i295\":\"not_shown\"},\"why\":\"The evidence does not include NVIDIA management's claim of accelerating growth as quarterly revenue approaches $100 billion.\"}\n{\"control\":24,\"same_question\":\"no\",\"same_due\":\"no\",\"items\":{\"i100\":\"shown\",\"i179\":\"shown\",\"i181\":\"shown\",\"i101\":\"shown\",\"i197\":\"shown\"},\"why\":\"The judged question asks for NVIDIA-confirmed customer shipments by the end of 2028, while the ruler asks whether shipments began by the end of 2027.\"}"}}
